# Testing and quality

- Prefer behavior tests over implementation-detail tests.
- Use pytest and pytest-django. Keep tests deterministic; freeze time where lifecycle behavior depends on time.
- Each feature tests: permissions/ownership, validation boundaries, state transitions, failure behavior, and the primary happy path.
- Add database constraint tests for critical invariants.
- Add query-count or query-shape tests to high-traffic lists and staff queues when regressions are plausible.
- Webhook and scheduled work must test duplicates, replay, out-of-order delivery, partial failure, and retry.
- Upload tests must use hostile filenames, wrong MIME/magic bytes, oversized dimensions, metadata, duplicate/reordered images, and unauthorized object keys.
- Search tests cover state/county scope, category/vertical filters, visibility, featured placement, sorting, pagination, and malformed query values.
- UI tests cover form errors and critical end-to-end flows; do not use browser tests for every branch that can be covered lower in the pyramid.
- Tests may not call real Stripe, SMS, email, S3, or AWS endpoints.
- A changed behavior is incomplete until the relevant tests are added or the feature spec documents why existing coverage is sufficient.
- Do not weaken assertions, skip tests, or lower coverage solely to make CI pass.
